#For local run
First install Docker toolbox if on Windows Home
Run: docker-machine start default
Check with: docker-machine ls

Useful commands:
- docker-machine ls
- docker ps
- docker ps -a
- docker stop <container name>
- docker rm <container name>
- docker images
- docker rmi <image name>
- docker run -p 80:5555 <image name>
- docker system prune

- docker run -d <image name> : run in background
- docker attach <id>

-docker history <image name>